; La Aventura Original, part two: getting in, and what the first part left in
; your hands.
;
; Two things have to be right for the inventory to be, and neither was. The
; adventure answers INVENTARIO with "> I _ PROCESS 10", and I is a noun of
; value 14, so the word only reaches that entry if a verbless sentence promotes
; its noun to the verb. Then, with the entry reached, it tests NOTZERO 1 — flag
; 1 is how many objects are carried — and a RESET that put the objects back
; without putting the count back answered "you have nothing" with the lamp, a
; key, the food and the water in hand.
;
;   qdaad compile -i examples/AO/ZXSpectrum/+3/part2/game.sce -m pc -s vga -f ddb -o tmp/AO2 --part 2
;   qrun -i tmp/AO2.ddb -T examples/AO/test/part2.qtest

TEST "La Aventura Original, part two, entered"

SEED 1989

INCLUDE "prologue.qtest"

STEP "the first room of the second part"
  EXPECT "Los rayos del sol"
END

STEP "and what the first part handed over"
  INPUT  i

  EXPECT "Una llave"
  EXPECT NOT "No tienes nada"
  ASSERT FLAG 1 > 0
END

STEP "what is put down leaves the hand, and the count with it"
  INPUT  dejar moneda
  EXPECT "Has dejado la moneda"

  INPUT  i
  EXPECT NOT "moneda"
END

STEP "and nothing in that reached a condact we have not written"
  EXPECT NOT "not implemented"
END
